  <p>The Policies &amp; Procedures module governs the document lifecycle, from registration through to publication.</p>

  <h2>Records</h2>
  <p>Five types, each with its own tab and journey: <strong>Policies</strong> and <strong>Forms</strong> (title, description, scope, ownership), <strong>Procedures</strong> (level 3 of the Process Architecture: filed under a level-2 process, with the procedure card), <strong>Services</strong> (the service card: type, requirements, beneficiaries, channels, providing and participating units) and <strong>Glossary</strong> terms (a term and its definition). The code and version are assigned by the system: type - unit - number - version, for example POL-HR-001-V1.</p>
  <p><strong>Update existing</strong> opens the next version as a draft carrying everything forward; a reason for change is required. A published record is read-only.</p>

  <h2>The Documenter</h2>
  <p>Policies, forms and services go through: Data Verification (the verifier chosen when the record was logged) → Approved Addition (the P&amp;P Manager) → Initial Draft Preparation (the owning unit's head hands it to a reporter, who writes the clauses and sends it back) → Initial Draft Review (the P&amp;P Manager, clause by clause) → Stakeholder Review (the chosen unit heads approve or reject from their own worklist; green / red / orange, sequence groups, auto-approval after a silence period in working days, skip when there are no stakeholders) → Final Approval (the chosen heads) → Send for Publishing (a publisher pastes the link and the manager confirms, or publish in the system only) → Published.</p>
  <p>Procedures follow the same stages with two differences: in Initial Draft Preparation the steps are written instead of clauses, and after Stakeholder Review come Procedure Design (drawn from the steps; a change to the drawing changes the steps and back) and Design Review. A glossary term needs only the P&amp;P Manager's approval and is then visible to everyone.</p>
  <p>Time in each stage is measured automatically in working days, skipping the non-working days and holidays set in Settings.</p>

  <h2>The document and publishing</h2>
  <p>From any record, choose <strong>View document</strong> for a document carrying your company's logo: cover, definitions, scope or clauses or the procedure card or the service card, the diagram, steps and operational authorities for procedures, classification, change log and approvals. An unpublished document carries a draft line with its stage. On publishing, a PDF is generated and filed in the owning unit's Library folder, and everyone is notified.</p>

  <h2>Efficiency Evaluation</h2>
  <p>The evaluation scores how complete a process is across six dimensions and returns recommendations.</p>

  <div class="tip">Everything in the document comes from record data. If a section is missing, fill it in on the record or in the Documenter rather than in the document.</div>
<% end %>
